name w3-05-emcon-1
timeout 520
time 1991-01-19T00:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN W3, SORTIE 5 OF 10 - THE DEFENCE'S OWN ANSWER: EMISSION DISCIPLINE AGAINST A PACKAGE.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w3-desert-storm.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: w3-03-weasel-close.fbm. THE ONE LINE THAT DIFFERS: the battery's
# `set emcon free` -> `set emcon free 30 200` - a briefed emission plan, off the air at t = 30 s and
# back on it at t = 200 s. Nothing else in the file moves, the Weasels included.
#
# WHY THIS IS THE DEFENCE'S ANSWER AND NOT A TRICK. The anti-radiation round's memory is a RATE and
# never a POINT (doc/air-to-ground.md section 2.2): after the last reception the measured line-of-sight
# rate is held for `SeekerMemoryS` = 4.0 s and is then ZERO, so proportional navigation commands nothing
# lateral, the accelerometer's 1 g bias survives and the round coasts STRAIGHT. The miss it produces is
# the zero-effort miss of the guidance law already in the tree, so WHEN a crew goes dark decides the
# outcome CONTINUOUSLY. The escape boundary has been measured on the weapon's own proof geometry at
# 85.0 % of the round's flight for a 5 deg shot and 88.1 % for a 35 deg one; this file asks the
# different, campaign-scale question.
#
# THE ARENA, the net-as-buried-cable, the substitutions, the time separation of the two engagements and
# what NIGHT is worth are stated in w3-03-weasel-close.fbm and hold unchanged.
# WHICH DEFENSIVE LAYER THIS FILE MEASURES: the MISSILE layer. No fighter flies in 03, 04 or 05.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: WHAT IS A POSITION'S EMISSION DISCIPLINE WORTH AGAINST A PACKAGE - not
# against a single round, which the weapon's own proof missions already answer, but against a formation
# that has a suppression element AND strikers behind it?
#
# MEASURED (fingerprint f9a9770250eaa961), AND IT IS A TRADE WITH BOTH HALVES VISIBLE:
#   what it BUYS      `site GO_DARK why="emission plan"` at t = 29.9, i.e. at 57.4 % of the round's
#                     52.08 s time of flight. The AGM-88 coasts on and hits the ground at 44.1977,
#                     214 m short of a battery at 44.2000. `UNIT_RESULT unit=q5sa3 result=INTACT`
#                     against the control's DESTROYED. The margin is 214 m and it is the whole answer
#                     to "is 57 % early enough here": on THIS geometry, yes, and barely
#   what it COSTS     the battery gives up the engagement it was in. `site RADIATE why="emcon free"` at
#                     t = 200.0, first launch at t = 231.7 - 194 s after the control's first launch and
#                     172 s after the control's battery was already dead
#   what it BUYS BACK four V-601 at t = 231.7 / 234.3 / 265.0 / 267.5, at 25.7, 26.4, 33.7 and 34.3 km -
#                     and every one of them goes WEST at the DEPARTING WEASELS (brgDeg 268-270), not at
#                     the strikers. Zero arrivals. The battery survived, came back, and spent its
#                     magazine on the aircraft that were leaving
#   the objective     `mission SUPPRESSION_LOST ... emittingS=120 allowanceS=120` at t = 290.2: the
#                     cumulative emission crosses the allowance 170 s after the shutdown began, i.e.
#                     the crew paid its 170 s of silence and then spent it again
#   the strikers      2 of 2 released (t = 275.2 / 290.6), `q5tgt` DESTROYED, same tick and same miss
#                     distance as the control
# SO: EMISSION DISCIPLINE IS WORTH THE POSITION AND NOTHING ELSE. It survives, and in surviving it
# suppresses itself for 170 s - which is the `C26` distinction between SUPPRESSED and DESTROYED with
# numbers on both sides of it. `objective suppress unit q5sa3 emitting 120` is UNMET here (330 s of
# cumulative radiation) and MET in the control (60 s, because the site died): the verdict kind measures
# emission, and a crew that dodges one round and comes back has not been suppressed.
#
# WHAT TO READ:
#   events.log      `site GO_DARK why="emission plan"` t = 29.9, `UNIT_RESULT unit=q5wsa_agm88_1
#                   result=IMPACT ... lon=44.1977` (214 m short), `site RADIATE why="emcon free"` t = 200,
#                   then the four `site LAUNCH ... brgDeg=268..270`
#   telemetry_q5sa3.csv  site_state and site_launches, and the 170 s hole in the middle of them
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is expected and is not the measurement. THE MEASUREMENT IS THE TRIPLE
# (`UNIT_RESULT unit=q5sa3`, the launch count and its bearings, strikers that reached release) read
# beside w3-03 and w3-04. The 214 m is a MARGIN, not a rule: it is one shutdown time on one geometry,
# and the campaign does not generalise it into a percentage.

net kari5
  control q5nod
  link wire
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs free
  member q5nod
  member q5sa3 autonomy free
  member q5flk autonomy free

unit q5wsa
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight ws5 1
  spawn 33.20000 43.98500 5000 90.0 480
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 agm88
  set store 7 agm88
  set arm_class fire_control
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode arm
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  wp 33.20000 44.06000 5000 480
  wp 33.20000 43.40000 5000 480
  objective suppress unit q5sa3 emitting 120
  objective survive

